cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Kestrel: flagging radio frequency interference in radio spectrograms
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it as below, and cite the original
  U-Net RFI method of Akeret et al. (2017) that the baseline reproduces.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Singh Raina
    given-names: Ronak
repository-code: "https://github.com/RonakSinghRaina/MINOR-Project"
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
abstract: >-
  Pixel-wise flagging of radio frequency interference (RFI) in radio
  spectrograms with Kestrel, a U-Net-based network, compared with tf_unet
  (Akeret et al. 2017) and the methods published by Mesarcik et al. (2022) on
  real LOFAR data with expert test labels and on simulated HERA data.
keywords:
  - radio frequency interference
  - RFI mitigation
  - radio astronomy
  - semantic segmentation
  - U-Net
  - deep learning
